{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32839 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Genipin 1-O-Beta-D-Isomaltoside appears to have a shared target relationship with LNCaP through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by two distinct compounds: one is 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and the other is Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside. All three of these compounds are linked to LNCaP, indicating a potential role in the regulation of this cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Genipin 1-O-Beta-D-Isomaltoside may influence LNCaP through the activation of downstream targets that are involved in cellular processes affecting the cell line. The evidence supports a network of interactions where Genipin 1-O-Beta-D-Isomaltoside could be a key player in modulating LNCaP through these intermediaries.",
